From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Turn camera previews upright on the hinge-down cover

The cover's rotation 0 is hinge up, so holding it hinge down is rotation
180. A camera buffer shows upright on a TextureView only at rotation 0
unless the app turns it, so apps that leave the transform alone showed the
camera upside down there and face checks failed (My VNPT's eKYC). SurfaceView
previews such as Samsung Camera's turn with the display and were fine.

Mark the SurfaceTexture behind each Camera2 output Surface once an
OutputConfiguration accepts it (all of them go through one). A new Surface
over the texture clears the mark, so video played into it later through a
new Surface is left alone. When a TextureView shows a marked texture on
display 0 at rotation 180, add a half turn to the layer transform. Apps
that handle rotation already turned it themselves (their matrix flips Y or
skews, or the view or a parent is rotated or flipped upside down), so they
are left alone. The app's own matrix and getTransform() stay as set.
Camera1 previews (setPreviewTexture) are not covered.

diff --git a/smali/android/graphics/SurfaceTexture.smali b/smali/android/graphics/SurfaceTexture.smali
